<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tang campaign against the Eastern Turks</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">630 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tang campaign against the Eastern Turks was a military expedition launched by Emperor Taizong that defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-turkic-khaganate">Eastern Turkic Khaganate</a> in 630 CE. The capture of its ruler brought the steppe peoples north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under Tang overlordship, and Taizong accepted the title of Heavenly Qaghan. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> present the campaign as a key step in Tang military expansion into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-asia">Inner Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tang-campaign-against-the-eastern-turks.jpg" alt="Tang campaign against the Eastern Turks" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tang_Tujue_War.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
